WEBVTT

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:05.790
No!

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.710
What happened?

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:11.470
She just went into this state
when the fighting stopped.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:12.670
What caused it?

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.240
I think it was the SARGs' shots.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.710
She was improving after the treatment.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:21.400
I guess you can't fix minds like machines.

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:35.320
I've given her a tranquilizer.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.450
She should be fine when she wakes up.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.220
What you said was wrong.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.200
The hypnotherapy and counseling
were supposed to cure...

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:50.840
...Harriet's traumatic responses
to the sounds of gunfire.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:55.540
Don't place too much faith in
medical science, Commander.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:00.170
The human mind is like a black box,
compared to the universe.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.760
We do our best, but there are
always unknown factors.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:10.450
You sound like a bad politician.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.370
You can think of me that way if you'd like.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:21.900
In any event, if we wanted to rectify
the problem completely...

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:26.010
...we would obviously
have to remove the cause.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.180
Are you talking about...

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.140
Of course.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:37.620
During the first "Close Encounter War",
Harriet was hit by eight metal shards.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:43.230
One of them, the one lodged
here in her cerebellum...

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.300
...threw her into a five-year coma.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:50.700
This could be the ultimate cause
of these after-effects.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:55.500
But you can't remove that, can you?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.410
Unfortunately not.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:03.550
The brain has wrapped around it
and it's a part of her body now.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.650
So there will always be a high possibility...

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.920
...that she'll react to war and fighting?

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.980
Sorry, but I'm afraid so.

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:20.930
I realize that this puts the EX-1 at risk...

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:26.640
...but maintaining the status quo
appears to be your best option.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:27.200
What?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.940
I haven't been able to prove it yet,

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:36.000
but after repeating various analyses
these past few months...

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:42.810
...I've come to believe that
these may be alien fragments.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.890
Alien?

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:49.760
The reason Harriet and the EX-1
can communicate...

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.700
...may be because of this.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.790
It might be possible.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:04.260
Isn't that remarkable?

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.300
It is.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.400
If you can prove it.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:29.060
First Lt. Dan Simmons
relinquishing his post at 1200.

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.230
Same here.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.950
First Lt. Guenevere Green...

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.400
Second Lt. Sue Harris...

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.670
...ready to relieve you.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.400
See you in 12 hours then.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.040
Did you write it?

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.980
The reply to your sister's mail.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.580
No, not yet...

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:46.530
Excuse me.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:50.990
What's that guy's problem?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.960
You used to be the cool guy
around here till he showed up.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:58.490
Just what...

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.200
Close all gates.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:09.390
The base is now restricted.

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.750
No one's allowed in or out.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.810
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:15.080
Captain!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:18.190
We've lost Harriet Bartholomew.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.850
Hattie?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:25.110
She disappeared from the medical center.

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.110
She left her ID card behind.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.300
She hasn't returned to her quarters?

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.190
She has not.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.000
She could have gotten lost somewhere.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.070
Or perhaps...

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.140
Kidnapped?

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.370
Impossible.

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.240
No, it isn't.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.240
Someone on the base took her?

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:52.940
Some of those military people
aren't very fond of Funeral.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:57.720
Even if there were spies around,
why kidnap the girl?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:58.860
In any event,

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:03.790
we have security searching
the base and immediate area.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:05.360
We'll wait for their report.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.830
We'll just sit around and drink tea?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.830
We should be looking with them.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.340
Be ready to scramble.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:15.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:16.630
Y-yes, ma'am.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.140
I'm going, too.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:25.950
Why don't you go take a nap?

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.210
You're off duty.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.870
I'm counting on that nose of yours.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.660
You found her?

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:56.010
Oh, you again?

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.450
Here.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.420
Great.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.630
No clues at all.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.560
I wonder what the commander's thinking.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:11.720
Eh?

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.560
Concerning Harriet.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.770
What about her?

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:20.140
Do you think she's only considered
a tool to control the EX-1?

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.400
And if she is?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.200
If so, then her security is going to get tighter.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.240
But the commander has a daughter if I recall.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:37.090
It's possible that she feels
like a mother to Harriet.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:38.310
I doubt it.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.890
She threw everything away for her career.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.590
Those feelings are gone.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:50.070
Why?

00:10:50.070 --> 00:10:52.470
Why do you do what she wants?

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:56.340
You kill Maki just like that...

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.430
Why do you do whatever this girl says?

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.840
Do you understand me?

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.280
Do you know what's around your neck?

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:13.720
I see.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:16.640
What is it?

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.730
I'm sure Harriet's still on the base.

00:11:19.730 --> 00:11:21.060
Why is that?

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.900
She has no place left other than Funeral.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.800
Also...

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.170
If she were in any kind of danger, Frank...

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:35.540
No, the EX-1 wouldn't just be sitting there.

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.300
She's here! Area C-A!

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.010
Wait!

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:51.270
What's the matter?

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.720
Can't take it anymore?

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:56.590
Tired of being scared all the time?

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.350
That's why you ran, right?

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.420
But then you realized.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.430
You have nowhere to go.

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.740
So all you could do was wander around.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.590
I'm right, aren't I?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.110
I can't tell if you shut up!

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.330
It'll be hard to get her in the air ducts.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:53.910
We can't close the hatches
if we don't know where she is.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:56.980
Captain.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:57.940
Ma'am.

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:00.910
Take over a while, would you?

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.260
Go a little slower, all right?

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:37.720
Continue the search in D-Block.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:43.050
I can't believe she went in there.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.400
Commander, be careful!

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:14.440
There's a...

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:51.650
Where are you, Harriet?

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.290
Harriet.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:21.820
It's okay now.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.220
Just relax.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:26.960
We were all worried.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.400
You disappeared so suddenly.

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:35.100
But hide and seek is over now.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.740
Just wait there.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:38.450
No!

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:42.280
Stay away!

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.240
It's your life.

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:53.620
Follow your dreams.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:58.290
If you want to see us, come anytime.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:12.940
I hate being afraid!

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.540
Harriet...

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:22.150
I don't want to hear those
loud sounds anymore...

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:27.190
Those scary sounds that
took Mom, Dad, and Grandpa...

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.550
...away to the land of the fairies!

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:30.860
I'm sorry.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.730
Sorry you get scared.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:42.160
But we need your and Mr. Fairy's help.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.330
So please...

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:50.480
And if you stay with Mr. Fairy,
you can go to the land of the fairies.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.600
No, I can't!

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:54.900
There's no such place.

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.860
No land of the fairies!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.910
No, don't move!

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:08.690
Harriet!

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:43.520
Hattie...

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.300
Hey.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:55.070
Heard you came through pretty well.

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:58.830
What's with the tired face?

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:01.080
Don't worry about me.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:03.310
Same old mysterious guy.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:07.170
Want a ride?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.530
How to cure her problem.

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:30.740
How to remove the cause.

00:21:31.770 --> 00:21:34.000
The answer is difficult to find.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:39.440
But I realize what you need now.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:45.320
I did as you asked and talked to the manager.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:47.120
Thank you.

00:21:54.360 --> 00:21:56.630
Starting today, you'll live here.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:21:58.200
With me.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:21:59.930
With you?

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:00.900
That's right.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:06.910
But...

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.010
What about Mr. Fairy?

00:22:11.210 --> 00:22:14.080
Poor Mr. Fairy will be all alone.

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:16.750
Don't worry.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:21.490
We can go see him anytime.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.040
Loneliness and Sorrow

00:22:37.040 --> 00:22:40.240
Pure hatred. Orders to kill.

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:42.940
The ring that surrounds you craves murder.

00:22:42.940 --> 00:22:46.050
A prelude to eternity...

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:48.850
Next time,
Sorrow and Malice.
